  "id": "3249f8d9-6168-52ec-beff-af2b62cd9301",
  "slug": "we-be-jammin-jamaican-banana-bread",
  "name": "We Be Jammin\u2019 Jamaican Banana Bread",
  "recipe_type": "breakfast",
  "brief_description": "Coconut, rum and lime in banana bread? Yes, please! This is a delicious and tropical twist on the common and bland banana bread. So good you will never bake another run-of-the-mill banana bread! Serve this and watch the happy faces!",
  "cuisine": "Jamaican",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Lightly grease two 8x4 inch loaf pans."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Beat together 2 tablespoons of softened butter and cream cheese in a large bowl until fluffy. Slowly beat in sugar until well incorporated. Add the egg and mix well. Sift together the flour, baking powder, baking soda, and salt in a separate bowl. In a different bowl, mix together the bananas, milk, 2 tablespoons rum, lime zest, lime juice, and vanilla extract; stir well. Pour 1/3 of the flour mixture into the butter and mix well. Mix in 1/2 of the mashed bananas. Continue with another 1/3 of the flour, followed by the remaining banana mixture, and finally the remaining flour. Fold in 1/4 cup pecans and 1/4 cup coconut flakes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Pour the mixture into the loaf pans, and bake in the preheated oven until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean, about one hour. When finished, cool for 10 minutes in the pan, remove, and finish cooling on a wire rack."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "After you take the banana bread out of the oven, prepare the topping by stirring together the brown sugar, remaining butter, lime juice, and 2 teaspoons of rum in a small saucepan over medium-high heat. Bring to a simmer stirring constantly; cook until the sugar has dissolved and the mixture is smooth, about one minute. Remove from heat, and stir in 2 tablespoons pecans, and 2 tablespoons coconut. Spoon this topping over the loaves while they are still warm. The topping will harden slightly when the loaf cools."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 24,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 60,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 45,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
  "difficulty": "hard",
